# tally 2.1.8 P50, L §4.4 (group 4's fix review, z1; T's m2_g3_fix2_r3 fa, m2_gate8_window_moves fk_in, fk_z): a
# read is the window's hole only where its value depends on the day: a leg of known amount 0 adds 0.00 to flows of
# the place on whichever day, so fz is 0.00 as its windows each line fe. The count (nz) and the bound member (xz),
# which depend on the day, stay holes. dce84215 gave fz the window's hole.
# tally 2.2 (2.2-4): the clause `windows each` is cut; its asks are the plain line, the hole with each unknown day it
# carries named (`unknown day:`, 2.2-11). A caller who takes the window as one day pins its cell.
=== m.tally
model z1
  tally 2
  on 2026-08-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input w_zer: date
input zero: money PLN

move zer: transfers
  on w_zer
  leg cash from world to konto amount zero

ask fz: flows(konto, 2026-04-09 .. 2026-04-21)
ask fm: flows(zer, 2026-04-09 .. 2026-04-21)
ask nz: count(t in transfers over 2026-04-09 .. 2026-04-21)
ask bz: bal(konto, 2026-04-20)
ask xz: x.cash.amount for x in transfers over 2026-04-09 .. 2026-04-21
ask fe: flows(konto, 2026-04-09 .. 2026-04-21)


version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  w_zer = window(2026-04-15, 2026-04-25) "s"
  zero = 0.00 PLN "s"
  opening[konto] = 0.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "s"
=== expect
bz: ?"date within window(2026-04-15, 2026-04-25) not precise enough for a balance" (zer)
  unknown day: w_zer
  cut 2026-08-01
fe: 0.00 PLN
  cut 2026-08-01
fm: ?"date within window(2026-04-15, 2026-04-25) not precise enough for flows of zer" (zer)
  unknown day: w_zer
  cut 2026-08-01
fz: 0.00 PLN
  cut 2026-08-01
nz: ?"date within window(2026-04-15, 2026-04-25) not precise enough for a binding over transfers" (zer)
  unknown day: w_zer
  unfulfilled: zer
  cut 2026-08-01
xz (x = zer): ?"date within window(2026-04-15, 2026-04-25) not precise enough for a binding over transfers" (zer)
